    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0671" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v15/pg643"/>

                <head>351. Telegram From the Embassy in Egypt to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d351-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-05-16T13:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16, 1956—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2260… . Nasser working himself into state on believing … that decision taken
                    Paris that piecemeal supply armament to Israel by various nations would continue
                    until arms strength of Israel exceeded that of Arabs. He also being told past
                    reassuring statements by President<anchor n="2" xml:id="d351-f2"/> and
                        Secretary<anchor n="3" xml:id="d351-f3"/> part of cover plan to lull Egypt
                    into complacency this subject.</p>
                <p>We dismiss latter point saying these men of integrity who would not be party to
                    subterfuge. However believe it inevitable US in end will receive more blame than
                    France or other supplying nations.</p>
                <p>We doing indirectly what we can calm situation but are without record Paris
                    talks. Inclined to believe, whatever decision taken in Paris, would have been
                    best to have frankly informed Nasser rather than let him react to … perhaps
                    exaggerated … reports.</p>
                <p>Assume Department has kept in mind frequent predictions by this Embassy that any
                    appreciable arms to Israel will result in additional orders from Soviet bloc.
                    There is some reason to believe talks on this subject already underway with
                    Russians here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Byroade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d351-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d351-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 784A.56/5–1656. Secret; Priority.
                    Received at 7:19 p.m. Repeated to Tel Aviv, London, Paris, Amman, Baghdad,
                    Beirut, Jidda, and Damascus.</p>
            </note>
